\section*{Question 2}

The temperature, in degrees Celsius ( \({ }^{\circ} \mathrm{C}\) ), of the water in a pond is a differentiable function \(W\) of time \(t\). The table above shows the water temperature as recorded every 3 days over a 15-day period.
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Use data from the table to find an approximation for \(W^{\prime}(12)\). Show the computations that lead to your answer. Indicate units of measure.
\item[(b)] Approximate the average temperature, in degrees Celsius, of the water over the time interval \(0 \leq t \leq 15\) days by using a trapezoidal approximation with subintervals of length \(\Delta t=3\) days.
\item[(c)] A student proposes the function \(P\), given by \(P(t)=20+10 t e^{(-t / 3)}\), as a model for the temperature of the water in the pond at time \(t\), where \(t\) is measured in days and \(P(t)\) is measured in degrees Celsius. Find \(P^{\prime}(12)\). Using appropriate units, explain the meaning of your answer in terms of water temperature.
\item[(d)] Use the function \(P\) defined in part (c) to find the average value, in degrees Celsius, of \(P(t)\) over the time interval \(0 \leq t \leq 15\) days.
\item[(a)] Difference quotient; e.g.
\[
\begin{aligned}
& W^{\prime}(12) \approx \frac{W(15)-W(12)}{15-12}=-\frac{1}{3}{ }^{\circ} \mathrm{C} / \text { day or } \\
& W^{\prime}(12) \approx \frac{W(12)-W(9)}{12-9}=-\frac{2}{3}{ }^{\circ} \mathrm{C} / \text { day or } \\
& W^{\prime}(12) \approx \frac{W(15)-W(9)}{15-9}=-\frac{1}{2}{ }^{\circ} \mathrm{C} / \text { day }
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(b)] \(\frac{3}{2}(20+2(31)+2(28)+2(24)+2(22)+21)=376.5\) Average temperature \(\approx \frac{1}{15}(376.5)=25.1^{\circ} \mathrm{C}\)
\item[(c)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
P^{\prime}(12) & =10 e^{-t / 3}-\left.\frac{10}{3} t e^{-t / 3}\right|_{t=12} \\
& =-30 e^{-4}=-0.549^{\circ} \mathrm{C} / \text { day }
\end{aligned}
\]
This means that the temperature is decreasing at the rate of 0.549 °C/day when \(t=12\) days.
\item[(d)] \(\frac{1}{15} \int_{0}^{15}\left(20+10 t e^{-t / 3}\right) d t=25.757^{\circ} \mathrm{C}\)
\item[] \(2:\left\{\begin{array}{l}1: \text { difference quotient } \\ 1: \text { answer (with units) }\end{array}\right.\)
\item[] \(2:\left\{\begin{array}{l}1: \text { trapezoidal method } \\ 1: \text { answer }\end{array}\right.\)
\item[] \(2:\left\{\begin{array}{l}1: P^{\prime}(12) \text { (with or without units) } \\ 1: \text { interpretation }\end{array}\right.\)
\item[] \(3:\left\{\begin{aligned} & 1: \text { integrand } \\ & 1: \text { limits and } \\ & \text { average value constant } \\ & 1: \text { answer }\end{aligned}\right.\)
\end{itemize}
